Jihad: draw the text caret in the offscreen render.

PuppetWidget::JihadRenderDocument (added by 0005) called
nsIPresShell::RenderDocument with flags=0, which omits the caret. The Jihad
daemon renders web text fields for the on-screen keyboard, so a focused input
must show a visible cursor. Pass nsIPresShell::RENDER_CARET so RenderDocument
draws the caret when one would be visible (the editor is focused + the
embedding window is activated by the daemon). Scroll position is unaffected.

--- a/widget/PuppetWidget.cpp
+++ b/widget/PuppetWidget.cpp
@@ -705,8 +705,11 @@ PuppetWidget::JihadRenderDocument(nsIDocShell* aDocShell)
   // Render the current viewport (device pixels == CSS pixels here; default scale 1)
-  // straight into mDrawTarget, on a white background. flags=0 respects scroll pos.
+  // straight into mDrawTarget, on a white background. RENDER_CARET draws the text caret
+  // when an editable is focused (Jihad: the on-screen keyboard needs a visible cursor) —
+  // without it RenderDocument skips the caret entirely. Scroll position is still respected.
   nsRect r(0, 0,
            nsPresContext::CSSPixelsToAppUnits((float)w),
            nsPresContext::CSSPixelsToAppUnits((float)h));
-  nsresult rv = presShell->RenderDocument(r, 0, NS_RGB(255, 255, 255), ctx);
+  nsresult rv = presShell->RenderDocument(r, nsIPresShell::RENDER_CARET,
+                                          NS_RGB(255, 255, 255), ctx);
   return NS_SUCCEEDED(rv);
 }
